    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d49-a2">

                <pb facs="0080" n="46" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg46"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No. 56.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to General
                            de Castro Cerqueira.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Petropolis</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-11-08"><hi rendition="#italic">November 8,
                        1897</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: I have the honor to place in the
                    hands of your excellency the following copy of a telegram, which I have just
                    received from my Government: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Conger</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Minister.</hi></p>
                        <p>Express to the President our gratification at his escape, and our sincere
                            regrets and sympathy on account of the assassination of Marshal
                            Bittencourt.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sherman.</hi></p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>And in accordance with what I know to be the real sentiments of my Government I
                    beg, through your excellency, to make this expression to the President in the
                    fullest measure possible.</p>
                <p>Again, I improve the opportunity, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
